                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5e87640a-9d48-3f02-83e1-f992b1e5fff4",
                        "entry_id": "bca50781-6d82-3e09-8393-a87e55332596",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative spelling of boy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "alternative",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "465353a7-b57e-4ff2-beb5-c2c6d1cf197d",
                                "sense_id": "5e87640a-9d48-3f02-83e1-f992b1e5fff4",
                                "text": "The boi who has been my best friend, the cause of my pain, but never quite my lover is gone....I'm sitting here in his Radiohead \"don't tell me what kind of day to have\" tee (it smells like him) listening to WYIN, and trying not to cry."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "88a5be88-8a2c-4e30-8a26-a666ef1820e9",
                                "sense_id": "5e87640a-9d48-3f02-83e1-f992b1e5fff4",
                                "text": "And finally, in “Sk8er Boi,” Avril Lavigne tells us in her first two lines about the conflicts between the male and female by saying, “He was a boi, she was a girl, can I make it any more obvious.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d644378f-5e53-4353-8976-3e766449845f",
                                "sense_id": "5e87640a-9d48-3f02-83e1-f992b1e5fff4",
                                "text": "I inadvertently gave the afro-american delivery boi a $5 tip probably due to the fact that I had pickled a few brain cells."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bc94e64e-82c4-4d96-b4bd-9bd5ae1bebb9",
                                "sense_id": "5e87640a-9d48-3f02-83e1-f992b1e5fff4",
                                "text": "Try to count how many times the king [of Hyrule] says \"Mah Boi\", because I don't know."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ca92a63-09ae-40e1-9b77-33f8f5537e2b",
                                "sense_id": "5e87640a-9d48-3f02-83e1-f992b1e5fff4",
                                "text": "Bois lie, I can too / Revenge is my sweet tooth"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d93cff87-2272-3b96-9ed3-778883e0b274",
                        "entry_id": "bca50781-6d82-3e09-8393-a87e55332596",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A male bottom (i.e. submissive partner), defined not by junior age, but by his obedient role and submission to the dominant \\\"top\\\"."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "especially"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c728eba-4180-45c8-b6bb-242571b6bfcf",
                                "sense_id": "d93cff87-2272-3b96-9ed3-778883e0b274",
                                "text": "boi will be treated as a boi at all times and will find himself the recepitent ^([sic]) of many bare bottom spankings, private and in front of Daddies ^([sic]) friends."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f99b6a0-e5ae-4e89-8cc0-e73684546a96",
                                "sense_id": "d93cff87-2272-3b96-9ed3-778883e0b274",
                                "text": "You, tattooed, butch boi with experience and a leash."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "34227195-3b56-44cc-897f-a50325b7b21f",
                                "sense_id": "d93cff87-2272-3b96-9ed3-778883e0b274",
                                "text": "I fucked the boi that way. His ass had never known how good a man's dick feels when it's deep inside […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4ba65384-84f1-3415-9692-b6cccbf3326f",
                        "entry_id": "bca50781-6d82-3e09-8393-a87e55332596",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A lesbian who adopts a boyish appearance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8cc72452-e31d-4f62-8d21-e750d3f036c6",
                                "sense_id": "4ba65384-84f1-3415-9692-b6cccbf3326f",
                                "text": "So new that most people—most lesbians—over the age of 30 have no idea what a boi is. […] Most bois are in their twenties and have come of age in a time when women’s and gay rights seem like more of a given and less of an urgent struggle than they did to lesbians ten or twenty or more years older."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1e0c2adc-504c-380e-9862-93c9755c301b",
                        "entry_id": "bca50781-6d82-3e09-8393-a87e55332596",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A trans boy; a trans man or transmasculine person."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "neologism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "139e8d4d-1eb4-435f-94a8-6b09bb528881",
                                "sense_id": "1e0c2adc-504c-380e-9862-93c9755c301b",
                                "text": "For example, “queer” would include self-identified lesbians and gays who also have sex with the “opposite sex,” sexual practices and relationships that include kink, s/m, polyamory, and pansexuality, gender play and fuck including femmes and those feminine of center, butches and those masculine of center, queens, femboys, gurls, bois, sissies, tomboys, crossdressers, drag queens and kings, and genderfluid people."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
